WEBVTT

00:00.670 --> 00:02.540
- [Instructor] We're asked
which of these strategies

00:02.540 --> 00:03.690
would eliminate a variable

00:03.690 --> 00:04.990
in the system of equations?

00:04.990 --> 00:08.420
Choose all answers that apply.

00:08.420 --> 00:11.010
So this first one says add the equations.

00:11.010 --> 00:11.843
So pause this video.

00:11.843 --> 00:14.870
Would adding the equations
eliminate a variable

00:14.870 --> 00:16.630
in this system?

00:16.630 --> 00:18.770
All right, now let's do it together.

00:18.770 --> 00:21.630
So if we add these equations,

00:21.630 --> 00:23.190
we have, on the left hand side,

00:23.190 --> 00:24.850
we have five x plus five x,

00:24.850 --> 00:26.480
which is going to be 10 x,

00:26.480 --> 00:29.340
and then you have negative
three y plus four y

00:29.340 --> 00:32.090
which is just a positive
one y or just plus y

00:32.090 --> 00:34.360
is equal to negative three plus six,

00:34.360 --> 00:37.490
which is just going to be
equal to positive three.

00:37.490 --> 00:39.570
We haven't eliminated any variables,

00:39.570 --> 00:42.530
so choice A, I could rule out.

00:42.530 --> 00:45.550
That did not eliminate a variable.

00:45.550 --> 00:47.660
Let me cross it out and not check it.

00:47.660 --> 00:50.600
Subtract the bottom equation from the top.

00:50.600 --> 00:53.280
Well when we subtract
the bottom from the top,

00:53.280 --> 00:55.400
five x minus five x,

00:55.400 --> 00:58.970
that's going to be zero x's,
so I won't even write it down,

00:58.970 --> 01:00.890
and we've already seen
we've eliminated an x

01:00.890 --> 01:03.000
so I'm already feeling
good about choice B,

01:03.000 --> 01:05.780
but then we can see negative
three y minus four y

01:05.780 --> 01:07.340
is negative seven y.

01:07.340 --> 01:10.810
Negative three minus six is
going to be negative nine

01:10.810 --> 01:15.740
and so choice B does
successfully eliminate the x's.

01:15.740 --> 01:18.073
So I will select that.

01:20.240 --> 01:23.470
Choice C, multiply the
top equation by two,

01:23.470 --> 01:25.440
then add the equations.

01:25.440 --> 01:26.273
Pause the video.

01:26.273 --> 01:28.980
Does that eliminate a variable?

01:28.980 --> 01:31.400
Well we're gonna multiply
the top equation by two

01:31.400 --> 01:36.400
so it's going to become 10 x minus six y

01:37.000 --> 01:39.420
is equal to negative six,

01:39.420 --> 01:42.140
and you could already see if
you then add the equations,

01:42.140 --> 01:43.330
10 x plus five x,

01:43.330 --> 01:44.230
you're gonna have 15 x,

01:44.230 --> 01:45.620
that's not gonna get eliminated.

01:45.620 --> 01:48.610
Negative six y plus four
y is negative two y.

01:48.610 --> 01:50.120
That's not going to be eliminated,

01:50.120 --> 01:52.550
so we can rule that out, as well.

01:52.550 --> 01:53.883
Let's do another example.

01:55.140 --> 01:56.580
One, they're asking us the same question.

01:56.580 --> 01:58.290
Which of these strategies
would eliminate a variable

01:58.290 --> 01:59.740
in the system of equations?

01:59.740 --> 02:03.270
The first choice says multiply
the bottom equation by two,

02:03.270 --> 02:05.020
then add the equations.

02:05.020 --> 02:06.863
Pause this video, does that work?

02:07.890 --> 02:11.510
All right, so if we multiply
the bottom equation by two,

02:11.510 --> 02:13.410
we are going to get,

02:13.410 --> 02:14.310
if we multiply it by two,

02:14.310 --> 02:17.950
we're gonna get two x minus
two minus four y, I should say.

02:17.950 --> 02:20.700
Two x, I'm just multiplying
everything by two,

02:20.700 --> 02:22.470
minus four y

02:22.470 --> 02:23.890
is equal to 10.

02:23.890 --> 02:25.680
And then if we were to add the equations.

02:25.680 --> 02:27.670
Four x plus two x is six x,

02:27.670 --> 02:29.530
so that doesn't get eliminated.

02:29.530 --> 02:34.530
Positive four y plus negative
four y is equal to zero y,

02:34.550 --> 02:36.650
so the y's actually do get eliminated

02:36.650 --> 02:39.370
when you add four y to negative four y.

02:39.370 --> 02:42.670
So I like choice A and
I'm gonna delete this

02:42.670 --> 02:44.760
so I have space to work
on the other choices,

02:44.760 --> 02:46.440
so I like one.

02:46.440 --> 02:47.460
What about choice B?

02:47.460 --> 02:49.123
Pause the video, does that work?

02:50.050 --> 02:52.010
Multiply the bottom equation by four,

02:52.010 --> 02:55.490
then subtract the bottom
equation from the top equation.

02:55.490 --> 02:58.500
All right, let's multiply
the bottom equation by four.

02:58.500 --> 02:59.810
What do we get?

02:59.810 --> 03:03.770
We're going to get four x minus eight y

03:04.760 --> 03:07.470
is equal to 20, yup.

03:07.470 --> 03:08.940
We multiplied it by four

03:08.940 --> 03:12.720
and then subtract the bottom
equation from the top.

03:12.720 --> 03:16.040
So we would subtract four x from four x.

03:16.040 --> 03:17.030
Well that's looking good.

03:17.030 --> 03:18.320
That would eliminate the x's,

03:18.320 --> 03:20.520
so I'm feeling good about choice B.

03:20.520 --> 03:23.670
And then we could see if we
subtract negative eight y

03:23.670 --> 03:26.720
from four y, well, subtracting
a negative's the same thing

03:26.720 --> 03:28.900
as adding a positive,

03:28.900 --> 03:30.720
so that would actually get us to 12 y

03:30.720 --> 03:34.330
if we're subtracting
negative eight y from four y.

03:34.330 --> 03:37.000
And then if we subtract
20 from negative two,

03:37.000 --> 03:38.100
we get to negative 22,

03:38.100 --> 03:40.740
but we see that four x minus four x

03:40.740 --> 03:42.470
is going to eliminate our x's,

03:42.470 --> 03:45.270
so that does definitely
eliminate a variable,

03:45.270 --> 03:47.843
so I like choice B.

03:48.930 --> 03:50.490
Now what about choice C?

03:50.490 --> 03:52.540
Multiply the top equation by 1/2,

03:52.540 --> 03:54.140
then add the equations.

03:54.140 --> 03:56.470
Let's try that out, pause the video.

03:56.470 --> 03:59.300
All right, let's just multiply times 1/2,

03:59.300 --> 04:01.360
so the left hand side times 1/2,

04:01.360 --> 04:03.370
we distribute the one half
is one way to think about it.

04:03.370 --> 04:06.210
Four x times 1/2 is going to be two x

04:06.210 --> 04:09.312
plus four y times 1/2 is two y

04:09.312 --> 04:10.890
is equal to negative two times 1/2

04:10.890 --> 04:12.690
is equal to negative one.

04:12.690 --> 04:15.570
Now and then they say add the equations.

04:15.570 --> 04:20.120
So two x plus x is going to be three x,

04:20.120 --> 04:22.760
so that's not going to eliminate the x's.

04:22.760 --> 04:26.160
Two y plus negative two y,

04:26.160 --> 04:28.350
well that's going to be no y's.

04:28.350 --> 04:30.710
So that actually will eliminate the y's,

04:30.710 --> 04:32.800
so I like this choice, as well.

04:32.800 --> 04:35.320
So actually, all three of these strategies

04:35.320 --> 04:37.510
would eliminate a variable
in the system of equations.

04:37.510 --> 04:38.480
This is useful to see

04:38.480 --> 04:41.636
'cause you can see there's
multiple ways to approach

04:41.636 --> 04:44.890
solving a system like
this through elimination.

04:44.890 --> 04:46.140
Let's do another example.

04:48.110 --> 04:50.260
Which of these strategies
would eliminate a variable

04:50.260 --> 04:51.220
in the system of equations?

04:51.220 --> 04:52.600
Same question again.

04:52.600 --> 04:53.433
So the first one,

04:53.433 --> 04:55.330
they suggest to subtract
the bottom equation

04:55.330 --> 04:56.390
from the top equation.

04:56.390 --> 04:58.053
Pause this video, does that work?

04:59.300 --> 05:02.880
Well if we subtract the
bottom from the top,

05:02.880 --> 05:05.180
so if you subtract a negative two x,

05:05.180 --> 05:07.127
that's the same thing as adding two x,

05:07.127 --> 05:09.490
'cause you're adding two x
to three x, that's five x.

05:09.490 --> 05:11.350
The x's don't get eliminated.

05:11.350 --> 05:14.430
Subtracting four y from negative
three y's just gonna get us

05:14.430 --> 05:15.900
to negative seven y.

05:15.900 --> 05:17.510
The y's don't get eliminated,

05:17.510 --> 05:18.820
so I would rule this one out.

05:18.820 --> 05:20.750
Nothing's getting eliminated there.

05:20.750 --> 05:22.940
Multiply the top equation by three,

05:22.940 --> 05:25.070
multiply the bottom equation by two,

05:25.070 --> 05:26.510
then add the equations.

05:26.510 --> 05:28.880
Pause the video, does that work?

05:28.880 --> 05:31.380
All right, so if I multiply
the top equation by three,

05:31.380 --> 05:35.180
I'm going to get nine x minus nine y

05:35.180 --> 05:36.880
is equal to 21,

05:36.880 --> 05:39.890
and then if I multiply the bottom by two,

05:39.890 --> 05:41.480
so this is times two,

05:41.480 --> 05:46.150
I'm going to get two times
negative two is negative four x

05:46.150 --> 05:50.060
plus eight y is equal to 14,

05:50.060 --> 05:52.090
and then they say add the equations.

05:52.090 --> 05:54.070
Well if I add nine x to negative four x,

05:54.070 --> 05:55.480
that doesn't eliminate the x's.

05:55.480 --> 05:57.240
That gets me to positive five x,

05:57.240 --> 06:00.610
and if I add negative nine
y to a positive eight y,

06:00.610 --> 06:02.040
that also doesn't eliminate the y's.

06:02.040 --> 06:03.740
That gets me to a negative y,

06:03.740 --> 06:08.630
so choice B, I can also rule out.

06:08.630 --> 06:09.830
Once again deleting all of this

06:09.830 --> 06:12.513
so I have space to try
to figure out choice C.

06:13.390 --> 06:15.600
Multiply the top equation by two,

06:15.600 --> 06:17.830
multiply the bottom equation by three,

06:17.830 --> 06:19.090
then add the equation.

06:19.090 --> 06:20.740
So they're telling us to
do it the other way around.

06:20.740 --> 06:23.680
Pause the video, does this work?

06:23.680 --> 06:26.600
All right, so we multiply
the top equation by two

06:26.600 --> 06:29.460
and we're gonna multiply the
bottom equation by three.

06:29.460 --> 06:30.960
So the top equation times two

06:30.960 --> 06:35.170
is going to be six x minus six y

06:35.170 --> 06:37.530
is equal to,

06:37.530 --> 06:40.210
is equal to 14.

06:40.210 --> 06:41.640
And then with this bottom equation,

06:41.640 --> 06:43.940
when you multiply it by three, both sides,

06:43.940 --> 06:45.570
that's the only way to
ensure that the equation

06:45.570 --> 06:47.320
is saying the same thing
is if you do the same thing

06:47.320 --> 06:48.153
to both sides.

06:48.153 --> 06:50.040
That's really the heart of algebra.

06:50.040 --> 06:53.790
So negative two times
three is negative six x,

06:53.790 --> 06:55.550
and I already like where this is going,

06:55.550 --> 06:56.383
'cause when I add these two,

06:56.383 --> 06:58.360
they're going to get eliminated,

06:58.360 --> 07:02.160
plus four y times three
is gonna be plus 12 y

07:02.160 --> 07:04.650
is going to be equal to 21.

07:04.650 --> 07:06.100
And then they say add the equations,

07:06.100 --> 07:09.080
well, you immediately see
when you add the x terms

07:09.080 --> 07:10.150
on the left hand side,

07:10.150 --> 07:11.770
they are going to cancel out.

07:11.770 --> 07:14.773
So I like choice C.
